The Parapper build keeps each lexicon entry's surface, left ID, right ID,
and word cost. Connection costs are stored in the compact format generated
by Vibrato's v0.5.0 mecab_smalldic procedure. UniDic feature columns are
reduced to the four ASCII digits used by Morph boundary detection. The
four-digit feature encoding is not reversible to the original feature text.
Unlike Vibrato's precompiled release asset, this build does not apply the
BCCWJ CORE-trained connection-ID mapping.

